---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getLangFromUrl, t } from '../i18n/utils';

const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
---

<BaseLayout title={t(lang, 'legal.privacy.pageTitle')} description={t(lang, 'legal.privacy.description')}>
  <section class="py-[var(--spacing-section)]">
    <h1 data-animate="0" class="text-hero-h1 font-heading font-bold text-chill-text mb-12">
      {t(lang, 'legal.privacy.title')}
    </h1>

    <div data-animate="150" class="space-y-10 text-body-sm text-chill-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
      <!-- 1. Data Controller -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          1. Data Controller
        </h2>
        <p>
          The data controller is an individual, publisher of the Chill website and the ChillShell and Chill applications.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Contact: <a href="mailto:chill_app@outlook.fr" class="text-chill-accent hover:text-chill-accent-hover transition-colors">chill_app@outlook.fr</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 2. Data Collection -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          2. Data Collection
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our applications (ChillShell and Chill) do not collect, transmit, or store any personal data on external servers. They operate entirely on your device. No analytics, tracking, or telemetry data is sent to our servers or any third party.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If anonymous analytics are added in the future (e.g., via Plausible Analytics), this policy will be updated accordingly. Plausible is a privacy-focused, cookie-free analytics tool that does not collect personal data.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3. Local Data Storage -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          3. Local Data Storage
        </h2>
        <p>
          All data is stored locally on your device using secure mechanisms:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 pl-2 mt-3">
          <li>SSH keys are encrypted using AES-CBC (Android) or stored in the Keychain (iOS)</li>
          <li>The master encryption key is stored in the device's hardware-backed keystore</li>
          <li>PIN codes are hashed with PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 (100,000 iterations) and never stored in plaintext</li>
          <li>Session credentials remain on your device and are never transmitted</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong>Retention period:</strong> your data remains on your device as long as the application is installed. It is deleted when you uninstall the application or clear its data.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 4. Third Parties -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          4. Third Parties
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our applications do not share, sell, or transmit any data to third parties. SSH connections are established directly between your device and the remote server you configure. No intermediary server is involved.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 5. SSH Connections -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          5. SSH Connections
        </h2>
        <p>
          When you connect to a remote server via SSH, the connection is established directly between your device and the target server. The application does not route, intercept, or log the content of your SSH sessions. Host key verification uses a Trust On First Use (TOFU) model, and keys are held in memory only during active sessions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 6. Device Permissions -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          6. Device Permissions
        </h2>
        <p>
          The applications may request the following permissions, used solely for their core functionality:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 pl-2 mt-3">
          <li>Network access: required for SSH connections and Wake-on-LAN</li>
          <li>Biometric sensor: used for biometric authentication (optional)</li>
          <li>Local storage: used to store encrypted credentials</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- 7. Hosting and International Transfers -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          7. Hosting and International Transfers
        </h2>
        <p>
          This website is hosted by Vercel Inc. (United States). As part of hosting, Vercel may process technical data (IP address, access logs) in accordance with its own privacy policy.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Our applications do not transmit any personal data to servers. All data remains on your device.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 8. Your Rights (GDPR) -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          8. Your Rights (GDPR)
        </h2>
        <p>
          Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you have the following rights:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 pl-2 mt-3">
          <li>Right of access (Article 15)</li>
          <li>Right to rectification (Article 16)</li>
          <li>Right to erasure (Article 17)</li>
          <li>Right to restriction of processing (Article 18)</li>
          <li>Right to data portability (Article 20)</li>
          <li>Right to object (Article 21)</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Since our applications collect no personal data, there is no data to access, rectify, or delete on our end. All your data is exclusively on your device, under your full control.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          For any request: <a href="mailto:chill_app@outlook.fr" class="text-chill-accent hover:text-chill-accent-hover transition-colors">chill_app@outlook.fr</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 9. Complaints -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          9. Complaints
        </h2>
        <p>
          If you believe that your data is not being processed in compliance with regulations, you may file a complaint with the CNIL (French Data Protection Authority):
          <a href="https://www.cnil.fr" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-chill-accent hover:text-chill-accent-hover transition-colors">www.cnil.fr</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 10. Changes -->
      <div class="rounded-chill border border-chill-border bg-chill-elevated p-6">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-heading font-semibold text-chill-text mb-3">
          10. Changes
        </h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated at any time. The date of the last update is indicated below. We encourage you to review it periodically.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Last updated -->
      <p class="text-micro text-chill-text-muted text-center pt-4">
        Last updated: February 13, 2026
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
